# Whether every member of an interval of the round-up interval is positive: 0 < -xn, written xn < 0
# (xn is never -inf, and a NaN makes it false for the empty set); the default interval_positive_1 on
# the meaning. Exact, in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and
# comparisons"). Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of
# docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_positive_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       certain m lt 0 x x=xu,xn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the negated lower bound compared with 0 (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardPredicates.v upward_positive_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand
unused:        xu the negated lower bound alone tells: every member is at least -xn, and the state is empty exactly when it is a NaN

m = lt(xn, 0)
